<Base title="Method, disclosure & corrections" description="TengriChecker's evidence standards, publication disclosure, corrections contact, and terms of service.">
  <article class="check prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accountability</p>
    <h1>A catalogue of claims.<br />A record you can check.</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">TengriChecker catalogues reviewed public claims by Tengri. Each case is one page, with a focused response and expandable evidence for each claim. The catalogue currently contains the SCHIFFY fleet case and the Jihoz hacked-wallet case.</p>
    <h2 id="method">How we check</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One claim, one ruling.</strong> We split a thread into separate claims, so an accurate figure can be credited even if the conclusion drawn from it fails.</li>
      <li><strong>Primary data first.</strong> We use transactions and logs from the chains involved, and link to them.</li>
      <li><strong>We don't hide awkward facts.</strong> If a fact is unhelpful to us and relevant to a ruling, we state it and answer it.</li>
      <li><strong>We say what is wrong.</strong> The label False — team response states our denial of the ownership and extraction accusations. It is separate from the blockchain findings. If the records contradict him, the label says Wrong. If he has not shown a claimed link, it says No proof shown. If we have not checked a figure, it says Not verified.</li>
      <li><strong>Claims, not the person.</strong> We check statements. We don't speculate about anyone's identity or private life, and we don't name wallet owners without proof.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="terms">Terms of Service &amp; Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service &amp; Privacy Policy</a> covers data collection, liability protection, and your rights under applicable data protection frameworks.</p>
    <h2>Scope of the record</h2>
    <p>The Jihoz hacked-wallet findings refer to Ronin records through November 3, 2026. The SCHIFFY findings refer to the November 2, 2026 snapshot. The launch dataset runs through block 104,549,114; the broader review runs through approximately block 104,580,486. Links to live explorers may show later activity.</p>
    <p>The main post is linked on each applicable claim. Follow-up quotes were supplied as pasted text; their original source links are still pending and they are labeled accordingly. We do not attribute those quotes to the linked main post.</p>
    <p>The full working evidence file is private. Public pages contain selected findings, source links and the launch dataset. They do not publish the team-side wallet address roster or personal wallet ledgers. As a result, the public materials alone do not reproduce every private link test. The expandable claim sections describe each test's scope and limits.</p>
    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
    <p>If a ruling is wrong, we'll fix it and note the change here. Tengri can respond to any ruling, and we'll publish that response on the page.</p>
    <p>Send the transaction or source that shows the error to: <a href="mailto:tengrichecker@proton.me">tengrichecker@proton.me</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
